{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#974","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#974","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#974\",\"parent_revision\":\"f10d67c2559f8231494f981d949e9255ac7a5e02\",\"root_revision\":\"106646efc46fb3a254faa03e0a36415e6e1ca69ae9edfb957becc5584f95f809\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd --worktree (-wt) flag to work-backlog-item, implement-feature, and start-task skills for opt-in git worktree isolation when working on individual tickets.\\n\\nCurrently worktree isolation is only used by /work-milestone during parallel wave execution. The user often works on multiple individual tickets manually and wants to avoid conflicts by choosing worktree isolation per-invocation.\\n\\nBehavior when --worktree is passed:\\n- work-backlog-item: passes the flag through to implement-feature when invoking it in Step 8.5a\\n- implement-feature: spawns each task agent with Agent(isolation: \\\"worktree\\\") instead of plain Agent()\\n- start-task: if invoked directly with --worktree, the agent runs in a worktree (the caller passes isolation: \\\"worktree\\\" to the Agent tool)\\n\\nBehavior when --worktree is NOT passed: no change from current behavior (agents work on main working tree).\\n\\nImplementation:\\n- Add --worktree to argument parsing in each skill's SKILL.md\\n- work-backlog-item: detect flag, pass through to implement-feature invocation\\n- implement-feature: detect flag, add isolation: \\\"worktree\\\" to Agent() calls in the dispatch loop\\n- start-task: no skill-level change needed \u2014 the isolation is set by the caller (implement-feature or manual Agent invocation)\\n\\nThe flag is orthogonal to /work-milestone \u2014 milestone execution always uses worktrees regardless of this flag.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add --worktree flag to work-backlog-item and implement-feature for opt-in isolation** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-21: user request for opt-in worktree isolation on individual ticket work\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Users working multiple tickets simultaneously have no isolation mechanism short of full milestone orchestration. This closes the gap between single-ticket interactive mode and the full /work-milestone pipeline without requiring milestone grooming overhead.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Developers who want per-ticket worktree isolation today cannot get it without using /work-milestone, which requires dispatch plan grooming.\\n- Bottleneck: The absence of opt-in isolation forces either serial ticket work (safe but slow) or unguarded parallel work (fast but conflicting). --worktree gives a third option.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables safe parallel single-ticket work without milestone overhead\\n- Gives the user explicit control over isolation \u2014 no implicit behavior change\\n- Reuses the same Agent(isolation: 'worktree') mechanism already proven in /work-milestone\\n- Keeps the flag orthogonal: /work-milestone always uses worktrees regardless of this flag\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `--worktree` is passed to `/work-backlog-item`, the flag propagates to `/implement-feature`, which then passes `isolation: 'worktree'` to every `Agent()` call in its dispatch loop. Each task agent runs in an isolated worktree branch. When `--worktree` is NOT passed, all agents run in the main working tree \u2014 existing behavior is preserved exactly.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- `work-backlog-item` SKILL.md: `--worktree` / `-wt` listed in the Arguments table and description frontmatter; flag detected and forwarded in Step 8.5a's `implement-feature` invocation\\n- `implement-feature` SKILL.md: `--worktree` listed as an optional flag; dispatch loop branches on flag presence \u2014 with flag: `Agent(isolation: 'worktree', ...)`, without flag: `Agent(...)` as today\\n- `start-task` SKILL.md: no change \u2014 isolation is set by the caller at the Agent() call site, not inside start-task itself\\n- `/work-milestone` behavior: unchanged \u2014 always uses `Agent(isolation: 'worktree')` regardless of this flag\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `/work-backlog-item --worktree #974` reaches implement-feature with the flag and all task agents are dispatched with `isolation: 'worktree'` in the Agent() call\\n2. `/work-backlog-item #974` (no flag) dispatches task agents without `isolation: 'worktree'` \u2014 existing behavior unchanged\\n3. `/implement-feature plan/P001-some-slug.yaml --worktree` dispatches all ready tasks with `isolation: 'worktree'`\\n4. `/implement-feature plan/P001-some-slug.yaml` (no flag) dispatches without isolation \u2014 existing behavior unchanged\\n5. Short form `-wt` is accepted as equivalent to `--worktree` in both skills\\n6. The `--worktree` flag does not affect `/work-milestone` \u2014 it still always uses isolation regardless\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:work-backlog-item \u2014 file: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md (Step 8.5a is the implement-feature handoff) |\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature \u2014 file: plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md (dispatch loop lines 67-93 is where Agent() calls are made) |\\n| Skill | /dh:start-task \u2014 file: plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md (no change needed \u2014 isolation is set by caller) |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone \u2014 file: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md (reference for how Agent(isolation: 'worktree') is used today) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/worktree-worker-protocol.md \u2014 full worker lifecycle with isolation |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md:253 \u2014 documents worktree isolation artifact access pattern |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 Agent(isolation: 'worktree') is already working in /work-milestone; this is a flag wiring exercise\\n- Blocks: #975 (TeamCreate dispatch option for /work-milestone) is a sibling concern for milestone-level dispatch; the two flags operate in different scopes and can be implemented independently\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The mechanism (Agent(isolation: 'worktree')) is already proven in /work-milestone. Changes are limited to: (1) adding flag parsing to two SKILL.md argument tables, (2) forwarding the flag in Step 8.5a of work-backlog-item, (3) branching the Agent() call in implement-feature's dispatch loop. No new infrastructure, no script changes, no schema changes.\\n\",\"digest\":\"35b58c4790167b7f6ff10ddbbcdbe3e8b84530326b2b45c45a7a39028c9e1e7d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgyEiw\"}"}